WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.143 --> 00:00:01.792
- Get ready for that puke shot.

00:00:01.792 --> 00:00:04.141
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.411 --> 00:00:08.827
- I'm definitely not a nutritionist,

00:00:08.827 --> 00:00:11.149
but I care about what my
kids eat and what I eat.

00:00:11.149 --> 00:00:12.984
- We get a calendar every month that lists

00:00:12.984 --> 00:00:15.886
the breakfast and lunch
that she gets at school,

00:00:15.886 --> 00:00:17.744
and it looks good.

00:00:17.744 --> 00:00:20.066
- I remember the cafeteria
lunches growing up

00:00:20.066 --> 00:00:23.526
being really bland and dry.

00:00:23.526 --> 00:00:25.151
- They tasted like cardboard.

00:00:25.151 --> 00:00:27.845
She's in the same school
district as I was, so

00:00:27.845 --> 00:00:28.913
hoping they improved.

00:00:28.913 --> 00:00:30.352
- I'm sure it'll be some
sort of combination of

00:00:30.352 --> 00:00:31.815
processed and heated foods

00:00:31.815 --> 00:00:34.184
and then maybe like a
token vegetable or fruit.

00:00:34.184 --> 00:00:38.131
(upbeat music)

00:00:38.131 --> 00:00:39.733
This is a substance I'm not familiar with.

00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:41.428
Can somebody tell me what this is?

00:00:41.428 --> 00:00:42.102
- See?

00:00:42.102 --> 00:00:43.425
Blob.

00:00:43.425 --> 00:00:44.865
And it smells like nothing.

00:00:44.865 --> 00:00:45.492
- Nothing.

00:00:45.492 --> 00:00:46.630
Just tastes like beige.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:48.696
- Seriously, this is
what they give at school?

00:00:48.696 --> 00:00:51.204
- It says fruits, grains,
vegetables, protein, dairy.

00:00:51.204 --> 00:00:53.433
My only question is is
if this is what we're

00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:55.755
supposed to be eating,
does this chicken salad

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.822
sandwich reflect that?

00:00:57.822 --> 00:01:00.673
(upbeat music)

00:01:02.373 --> 00:01:04.137
- I'm not excited about this.

00:01:04.137 --> 00:01:05.113
Not at all.

00:01:05.113 --> 00:01:07.249
- This is definitely
like a microwaved moment

00:01:07.249 --> 00:01:08.410
right now, I can tell.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.244
- Oh, it's so gross.

00:01:10.244 --> 00:01:11.986
- This sandwich looks like a scrotum.

00:01:11.986 --> 00:01:13.913
- The meatballs look like they can bounce.

00:01:13.913 --> 00:01:15.887
- This tastes like it was
prepared maybe a month ago.

00:01:15.887 --> 00:01:17.628
- I can plug my nose when I try it, right?

00:01:17.628 --> 00:01:19.885
- It bounced.

00:01:19.885 --> 00:01:21.367
- No one's seasoned this obviously.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:24.478
This is like tiny water
balloons in my mouth right now.

00:01:24.478 --> 00:01:25.941
- It tastes a little dish watery.

00:01:25.941 --> 00:01:27.148
- Very sad corn.

00:01:27.148 --> 00:01:27.915
- Where did they find this?

00:01:27.915 --> 00:01:29.424
Did it fall off a truck or something?

00:01:29.424 --> 00:01:31.723
- I would probably just eat these.

00:01:31.723 --> 00:01:34.397
(upbeat music)

00:01:35.577 --> 00:01:38.015
It's like a shoelace posing as meat.

00:01:38.015 --> 00:01:38.898
- Very pliable.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:40.152
- Aren't they supposed to be orange?

00:01:40.152 --> 00:01:42.265
- Why can't I pierce it
past a certain point?

00:01:42.265 --> 00:01:43.565
- Pretty bendy.

00:01:43.565 --> 00:01:44.563
- Is it really an egg?

00:01:44.563 --> 00:01:46.166
- That is disgusting.

00:01:46.166 --> 00:01:49.821
- I don't know what this
ham meat is supposed to be.

00:01:49.821 --> 00:01:52.342
- I wouldn't give that to my dog.

00:01:52.342 --> 00:01:53.248
- How is that meat?

00:01:53.248 --> 00:01:54.014
That's rubber.

00:01:54.014 --> 00:01:56.475
- Almost a fifth of
the entire day's sodium

00:01:56.475 --> 00:01:57.775
in this one packet.

00:01:57.775 --> 00:01:59.099
- That's so bad.

00:01:59.099 --> 00:02:02.210
How do children eat this?

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:04.532
It was actually way worse
than I thought it would be.

00:02:04.532 --> 00:02:05.995
- Everything felt a little rubbery.

00:02:05.995 --> 00:02:08.596
- I'm really worried that
this is what I depend on

00:02:08.596 --> 00:02:10.407
while I'm away from her.

00:02:10.407 --> 00:02:12.381
- I just think about the
kids who don't have access

00:02:12.381 --> 00:02:14.935
to meals and this is how
they're gonna eat lunch,

00:02:14.935 --> 00:02:16.700
and I'm just kinda bummed out

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.604
because this is what we're
offering them, and I think

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:21.112
we can do better, and we should do better.

00:02:21.112 --> 00:02:23.805
(peaceful music)

